@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Batch 32 authoring notes — Supersymmetry Ward Identities and Wilsonian Nonrenormalization
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+- Owned pair: `qftx-susy-ward-and-nonrenormalization` and `qftx-susy-ward-and-nonrenormalization-examples`, order 988, physics library, `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`.
+- The complete track section at lines 443–456 and current `plan-spec.json` rows agree on the A/B IDs, title, category, order, page-level requirements, and the N=1 Wilsonian claim. Batch 32 is level 5 and requires batches 4, 30, and 31 in `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json`.
+- The owner placement resolution in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/placement-review.md` moves `pthm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` to `aqft-susy-effective-theories`; this page retains only its distinct N=1 theorem, `pthm-qftx-n1-wilsonian-f-term-nonrenormalization`. The moved theorem is not authored or used here.
+- The dated prose scaffold says formal perturbative or regulated results do not establish a continuum theory, a generic interacting Wilsonian integration theorem, or arbitrary 1PI exactness. The new A-page definition therefore defines a conditional formal cutoff input and explicitly assumes its local derivative expansion; it claims no construction or convergence result.
+
+## Supplier inspection and current readiness
+
+- `qftx-nonabelian-brst-bv-mathematics` has a current A-page carrier. The exact used items are `def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex` and `lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence`. Their complete local statements/proof were inspected: the definition fixes the finite-dimensional Lie algebra, representation, ghost, and signs; the lemma proves square-zero on generators, jets, and the finite-jet algebra. `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` return `ready` for both. BRST nilpotence is used only for the declared gauge differential; it is not treated as a quantum anomaly-cancellation proof.
+- The math-foundation suppliers `def-qftx-superspace-grassmann-algebra` and `def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield` were inspected through the exact current item carriers. Their current readiness rows are `ready`. The first fixes the ordered generators, left/right derivatives, Berezin measures, and dimensions; the second fixes the flat superspace, chiral constraint, component expansion, and covariant derivatives.
+- The current N=1 page carrier `library/advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry/qftx-susy-n1-superspace-and-actions.md` is present, and all seven of its current items have closed `ready` Step 1 rows in the live snapshot. Its exact `post-qftx-n1-gauge-matter-model` is a classical SU(2) gauge-matter action with a gauge-invariant holomorphic superpotential and explicit coupling/trace conventions; it does not supply a generic Wilsonian quantum construction. The page uses the matter factor $e^{2gV_R}$ and $\mathcal W_\alpha=-\tfrac14\bar D^2(e^{-2gV_R}D_\alpha e^{2gV_R})$ with connection normalization. This batch uses $e^{-V_i}$ and $W_\alpha=-\tfrac14\bar D^2(e^{-V}D_\alpha e^V)$, with $g$ placed in $\tau$. No conversion between these superspace conventions has been derived or claimed, so the N=1 page-level edge remains `open`; its actual ready item carriers are not treated as proof of the generic quantum theorem.
+- The extended-actions page carrier is present. Its current postulates `post-qftx-n2-vector-hypermultiplet-model` and `post-qftx-n4-super-yang-mills-model` were read in full: they specify the selected SU(2) group, bundle, trace and coupling conventions; the N=2 model adopts eight-supercharge invariance, and the N=4 model adopts sixteen-supercharge invariance. Both are classical postulates and neither asserts a quantum measure. `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` reports a missing current Step 1 readiness record for each exact item carrier. The assigned page-level edge therefore remains `open`; this N=1 theorem makes no N=2 or N=4 deduction.
+
+## Sources read and fetched
+
+- Steven Weinberg, “Non-Renormalization Theorems in Non-Renormalizable Theories,” <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9803099v1>. The complete 13-page PDF was fetched and inspected. Read the action and Wilsonian form on pp. 1–3; the chiral/real spurions, R and theta-shift restrictions, and complete graph-counting argument on pp. 3–7; and the separate FI argument on p. 8. Harvested results: the N=1 Wilsonian F-term theorem (included in `pthm-qftx-n1-wilsonian-f-term-nonrenormalization`); the one-loop gauge-coupling exception and one-loop U(1) FI tadpole/charge-trace condition (included in the same item); and the perturbative/Wilsonian boundary (included as an explicit theorem caveat). `source-fetch-check --stamp` recorded 99,634 bytes, 13 pages, SHA-256 prefix `b7eff78d7b9226e4`; one fetch attempt succeeded.
+- Stephen P. Martin, *A Supersymmetry Primer*, version 7, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9709356v7>. The complete 160-page lecture-note PDF was fetched and inspected at §4.7 (printed p. 41), §4.10 (pp. 48–49), and §6.5 (pp. 66–67). Harvested results: the chiral action and distinction between holomorphic F terms and real Kähler/gauge-kinetic data (included in `def-qftx-wilsonian-n1-action-data`); the wave-function/anomalous-dimension relation for canonically normalized couplings (included in `ex-qftx-n1-wilsonian-wavefunction-vs-holomorphic`); and the D-term/Kähler qualification (included in the theorem). `source-fetch-check --stamp` recorded 1,723,786 bytes, 160 pages, SHA-256 prefix `b1dba94d82b75cc3`; one fetch attempt succeeded.
+- Searches and per-item dispositions are recorded in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-32.coverage.json`. Both sources fetched successfully; there are no retrieval failures, source drops, or `source_resolution` records.
+- The complete Weinberg text's count equation (12), after substitution of the two displayed end-count equations, gives $N_\tau=1-\tfrac12[\sum(m-2)\mathcal A_m+\sum(m+2-r)\mathcal B_{mr}+\sum m\mathcal C_m]$. Its following prose appears to print $\mathcal C_2=2$ for the one-vertex $m=2$ matter case; the preceding equation forces $2\mathcal C_2=2$, hence $\mathcal C_2=1$. The local proof uses the value derived from the equation and records this apparent source-text arithmetic inconsistency rather than repeating it.
+
+## Item authoring ledger
+
+### `def-qftx-wilsonian-n1-action-data`
+
+- Claim/conventions: defines a compact matrix-group N=1 superspace action on flat `(-+++)` Minkowski space, with fixed global form, finite-dimensional unitary matter representations, the holomorphic `e^{-V}` vector-prepotential/field-strength convention, formal holomorphic F and real D integrands, `tau = vartheta/(2 pi) + 4 pi i/g^2`, and a nonzero Wilsonian scale `lambda`. It defines the coefficientwise supersymmetry and BRST Ward identities, the real Kähler data, and the field-independent U(1) FI coefficient/charge trace. The selected 1PI cutoff vertex functional and local derivative expansion are explicit formal inputs, not results of generic interacting partial integration; no continuum or regulator-existence theorem is asserted.
+- Dependencies: `def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield`, `def-qftx-superspace-grassmann-algebra`, `def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex`, and `lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence`, all mathematical-premise edges. Their inspected item levels are 2, 0, 0, and 1 respectively, so this item has `dependency_level: 3`.
+- Decision: added as the missing local definition required before stating the Wilsonian theorem. It does not duplicate the SU(2)-specific model postulate or claim generic high-mode integration has been constructed.
+- Validation: source references are bound to both independently retrieved full texts and their exact locators. The complete current statement is synchronized into the batch manifest; final scoped checks are recorded below.
+
+### `pthm-qftx-n1-wilsonian-f-term-nonrenormalization`
+
+- Claim/conventions: coefficientwise nonrenormalization of the local holomorphic Wilsonian `F(Phi,W)` integrand under a formal rigid N=1 supersymmetric, gauge-invariant, anomaly-free regulator at nonzero scale and in the topologically trivial sector; only one-loop holomorphic gauge-coupling shifts are allowed. For each unbroken U(1), the field-independent FI coefficient receives only a one-loop correction proportional to the total left-chiral charge trace; field-dependent D-term operators remain distinct data. No Kähler, canonical-coupling, arbitrary 1PI, nonperturbative, or continuum conclusion is asserted.
+- Dependencies: `def-qftx-wilsonian-n1-action-data` (formulation prerequisite), `def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield` (mathematical premise), `def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex`, and `lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence` (mathematical premises). Their levels are 3, 2, 0, and 1 respectively, so this item has `dependency_level: 4`.
+- Decision: the action-data definition specifies the coefficientwise expectation and exact rigid-supersymmetry and BRST change-of-variables identities. The theorem takes those identities as assumptions and does not infer a quantum identity or anomaly cancellation from classical BRST nilpotence. The local proof follows Weinberg's chiral/real spurion, R/angle-shift, vector-line graph-counting, and separate constant-FI-tadpole arguments. The fixed canonical matter kinetic term supplies the counted matter vertices. Step 5.1 includes internal chiral matter lines in the loop count; the mixed cubic-gauge/$C_1$ graph has one loop but is one-particle-reducible through its vector bridge and is excluded by the stipulated vertex convention.
+- Validation: final scoped results are recorded below after all edits; the strict proof contract was regenerated for corrected step 5.1.
+
+### `ex-qftx-n1-wilsonian-wavefunction-vs-holomorphic`
+
+- Claim/conventions: in one chiral Wess–Zumino action with $W_0=\tfrac12m\Phi^2+y\Phi^3/3!$ and positive full kinetic coefficient $Z(\lambda)$, the theorem fixes the holomorphic $m,y$ while the field rescaling $\Phi_c=Z^{1/2}\Phi$ gives coefficients $m/Z$ and $y/Z^{3/2}$. The proof is a direct field rescaling; it does not assert that $Z$ must vary.
+- Dependencies: the local action-data definition (formulation prerequisite) and `pthm-qftx-n1-wilsonian-f-term-nonrenormalization` (physical result); maximum supplier level 4 gives `dependency_level: 5`.
+- Sources: Martin §6.5 supports the anomalous-dimension/canonical-coupling distinction; Weinberg equations (3)–(12) support the holomorphic Wilsonian conclusion. Both full-text stamps are in batch coverage.
+- Decision: authored as a conditional example with a complete algebraic verification; not a measured model or continuum result.
+- Validation: scoped proof-layout and item-contract checks remain pending.
+
+### `ex-qftx-n1-u1-fi-charge-trace`
+
+- Claim/conventions: for an unbroken compact U(1) with one left-chiral multiplet of charge +1 and one of charge -1, no superpotential ($F=0$), and no additional real interactions ($G=0$), the total charge trace vanishes, so the one-loop FI tadpole cancels and the theorem excludes higher-loop FI shifts. Other D terms remain unprotected.
+- Dependencies: the local action-data definition (formulation prerequisite) and the N=1 Wilsonian theorem (physical result); maximum supplier level 4 gives `dependency_level: 5`.
+- Sources: Weinberg's separate FI argument, pp. 7–8, supports the one-loop tadpole/charge-trace condition. The complete PDF fetch stamp is current.
+- Decision: authored as a conditional example with the charge sum computed explicitly; no empirical or continuum claim.
+- Validation: scoped proof-layout and item-contract checks remain pending.
+
+- The two page carriers are now frontmatter-only. The A inventory is the local action-data definition followed by the N=1 theorem; the B inventory contains both verified examples. The batch manifest, proof contracts, source coverage/stamps, and cross-batch rows are present; final structural checks and per-item Step-1 readiness recording remain.
+- Next action: rerun the exact manifest/contract/source/dependency checks after final source edits, recheck live supplier readiness, record ready/escalated dispositions without overwriting any escalation, and close this batch evidence.
